{title: 343 - I Will Sing of My Redeemer}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #343 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 343}
{meta: category Gospel - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]I will sing of my Re[D]deemer, And His [D7]wondrous love to [G]me;
[G]On the cruel cross He [D]suffered, From the [D7]curse to set me [G]free.
[G]Sing, oh [C]sing, of my Re[G]deemer, With His [D7]blood, He purchased [G]me.
[G]On the [C]cross, He sealed my [G]pardon, Paid the debt, and [D7]made me [G]free.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]Sing, [D]oh sing, [D7]of [G]my Redeemer,
[G]With [D]His blood, [D7]He [G]purchased me.
[G]On [C]the [G]cross, He [D7]sealed [G]my pardon,
[G]Paid [C]the [G]debt, and [D7]made [G]me free.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]I [D]will tell [D7]the [G]wondrous story,
[G]How [D]my lost [D7]estate [G]to save,
[G]In [C]His [G]boundless [D7]love [G]and mercy,
[G]He [C]the [G]ransom [D7]freely [G]gave.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]I [D]will sing [D7]of [G]my Redeemer,
[G]And [D]His heavenly [D7]love [G]to me;
[G]He [C]from death [G]to [D7]life hath [G]brought me,
[G]Son [C]of [G]God with [D7]Him [G]to be.
{end_of_verse}
